Z||000004||Haze_Performance||03-16-2001||01:39 AM||||I wouldnt take those numbers to serious. I was checking some out & they look to be incorrect.<P>The Mustang numbers are all worng.<P>1998 Ford Escort ZX2 (15.7 1/4mile) was faster than a 1993 Mustang GT? (16.1) <B>BS!!!</B><P><BR>And the 85 Mustang was the fastest Fox Body made.. But he has it as one of the slowest..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">   </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Penncok's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery</A>||||reg||13
Z||000005||99BlackZ||03-16-2001||08:11 AM||||I don't think those times are off by much.<BR>You have to remember a few things.<BR>Times depend on many factors.<BR>Driver skill, track conditions, weather conditions just to name a few.<P>As far as your mustang observations, I can speak from experience.  I am a mustang NUT having owned 6 of them. <P>The '85 was quick for it's time, but wasn't one of the fastest fox bodies.<BR>I love the '85, last carbuerated, first roller cam, headers, etc.<BR>But. . .Almost all of the Fuel injected stangs were faster with the fox body (stock).<P>Having owned 6 mustangs, 2 V-6 fieros and currently a 99ZX2, I can tell you that the Z is faster than most people think.  If you noticed the '93 Stang you were referring to was an Auto.  That makes a huge difference because the auto's on the stangs suck.  I thought the Z was faster than my fiero's but now I see the numbers to prove it.<BR>You have to remember the Z only weighs 2450lbs.  130hp. It is a quick little sucker (with a 5 sp.) but not a speed demon either.<BR>I bought mine for MPG though not MPH.<P>Shave 300lbs off the fiero and it would do wonders.<P>Now don't get me wrong and start flaming, I LOVE fieros.   Unfortunately, GM just didn't make them very fast out of the box.<BR>That's why engine swaps are so popular.<BR>What I love about fieros is they look great and you can do so many things with them.<BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||b lo 0||03-17-2001||01:45 PM||||Hey BlackZ, no offense, but Haze is no stranger to Mustangs either, and btw, 4 cyl fieros weighed in at 2,400 lbs, about 90 hp, and the '85 GT (the lightest GT) was about 2,600 lbs, 145 hp, 155 lb-ft, 0-60 7.3 sec with the 5 spd.  I may be a little off with the GT numbers, but I'm pretty close (I've had 2 '85 GT's).  BTW, ZX2's are fast, Ive seen a stock one beat a Civic SI with an exhaust and cold-air (I was IN the SI-my sister's boyfriend's).  OK, I'll shut up now.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">     <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!<P><A HREF="http://clubs.excite.com/welcome/main?cid=.zXb1DJ1lsCL&aid=22&auth=" TARGET=_blank>Pontiac Fiero Owner's Club</A>-Pics, Videos and More-Or Post your Own||||reg||1
Z||000007||88formula||03-17-2001||07:29 PM||||The Buick Park Avenue Ultra has a 225-240 horsepower supercharged 3.8-liter engine. The fiero has just 135 horsepower and it runs out of breath after 5000 rpm. I don't know why everyone thinks fiero's are rocket ships; they are not fast in stock form especially by today’s standards. They just provide average acceleration. The 8 second 0-60 time and the 16 second quarter mile time are correct. That is exactly what Dragstrip2000 comes up with for a time for a 5-speed fiero formula that weighs in at 2745 lbs. without the driver. The Factory rates an 88 fiero GT with the five-speed transmission as going 0-60 mph in 8.7 seconds and running the quarter mile in 16.4 seconds. A 5-speed Toyota Corolla can run 0-60 mph in 8.1 seconds and run the quarter mile in 16 seconds. Stock fieros at the track run low 16 seconds times and I have read on this forum that the guys with the 3.1-liter engines are only running high 15 second times. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||HAGS||03-17-2001||08:47 PM||||My Car: <BR>1991 <BR>Mercury Capri XR2<BR>8.3/16.3<P>Cars I've beat recently:<BR>1999<BR>Pontiac Grand Am GT(auto)<BR>7.7/15.9<P>1992<BR>Chevy Camaro 350(auto)<BR>?/?<P>1993<BR>Ford Mustang GT(auto)<BR>8.0/16.1<P>Cars I've lost to:<BR>1999<BR>Ford Mustang Cobra SVT<BR>5.4/13.9<BR>(out of my league)<P>1998<BR>Mazda 626 LX<BR>9.1/17.0<BR>(couldnt find 3rd gear)<P>1992<BR>Chevrolet Corvette ZR-1<BR>5.6/13.9<BR>(just outclassed)||||reg||1
